><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20251110101703+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20251110101714+10'00'" name="b170e53e-865d-4364-bd29-45f8b48c3160" page="15" coords="51.023605,349.220154,289.254822,349.220154,51.023605,334.130280,289.254822,334.130280,51.023605,336.720154,289.122833,336.720154,51.023605,321.630280,289.122833,321.630280,51.023605,324.220154,289.137390,324.220154,51.023605,309.130280,289.137390,309.130280,51.023605,311.720154,289.268402,311.720154,51.023605,296.630280,289.268402,296.630280,51.023605,299.220154,288.905670,299.220154,51.023605,284.130280,288.905670,284.130280,51.023605,286.720154,289.260651,286.720154,51.023605,271.630280,289.260651,271.630280,51.023605,274.220154,289.137451,274.220154,51.023605,259.130280,289.137451,259.130280,51.023605,261.720154,289.112488,261.720154,51.023605,246.630280,289.112488,246.630280,51.023605,249.220154,288.950562,249.220154,51.023605,234.130280,288.950562,234.130280,51.023605,236.720154,289.131042,236.720154,51.023605,221.630280,289.131042,221.630280,51.023605,224.220154,289.243744,224.220154,51.023605,209.130280,289.243744,209.130280,51.023605,211.720154,289.151367,211.720154,51.023605,196.630280,289.151367,196.630280,51.023605,199.220154,289.183685,199.220154,51.023605,184.130280,289.183685,184.130280,51.023605,186.720154,289.102936,186.720154,51.023605,171.630280,289.102936,171.630280,51.023605,174.220154,289.133514,174.220154,51.023605,159.130280,289.133514,159.130280,51.023590,161.720154,289.142456,161.720154,51.023590,146.630280,289.142456,146.630280,51.023590,149.220154,289.303558,149.220154,51.023590,134.130280,289.303558,134.130280,51.023590,136.720154,289.134766,136.720154,51.023590,121.630280,289.134766,121.630280,51.023590,124.220154,289.213135,124.220154,51.023590,109.130280,289.213135,109.130280,51.023590,111.720154,289.122620,111.720154,51.023590,96.630280,289.122620,96.630280,51.023590,99.220154,289.166229,99.220154,51.023590,84.130280,289.166229,84.130280,51.023590,86.720154,289.160278,86.720154,51.023590,71.630280,289.160278,71.630280" rect="50.552032,71.158722,289.775116,349.691711" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>This is the first systematic review and meta-analysis to&#xD;synthesise evidence on changes in biomechanical and neuromuscular&#xD;variables following CSE training in distance&#xD;runners. CSE training was found to significantly improve&#xD;knee flexion, ankle plantarflexion, knee extension and squat&#xD;strength more than endurance training alone, suggesting&#xD;an increased force-generating capacity in the triceps surae,&#xD;quadriceps, hamstring and gluteal muscle groups. These&#xD;muscles play a crucial role in centre of mass propulsion and&#xD;acceleration of the leg during running, and further research&#xD;is required to establish whether these adaptations in muscle&#xD;force transfer to larger stride lengths and faster running&#xD;speeds. CSE training may also have beneficial effects for&#xD;drop jump RSI and triceps surae tendon stiffness during an&#xD;ankle plantarflexion contraction, but caution should be exercised&#xD;when interpreting the results of the existing literature&#xD;because adaptations may be task-dependent. These results&#xD;highlight the need to investigate how adaptations to CSE&#xD;training transfer to overground running and how distance&#xD;running kinematics and kinetics change following a period&#xD;of CSE training. Improved understanding of these mechanisms&#xD;can have important implications for the prescription </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>of strength training and taper periods in preparation for&#xD;competition.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="15" rect="595.276001,257.220154,779.276001,349.220154"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20251110101046+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20251110101054+10'00'" name="445cbdc7-4550-4423-9ed1-9512d4f10d18" page="17" coords="88.342789,231.411804,128.938690,231.411804,88.342789,218.107910,128.938690,218.107910,51.023605,230.327759,86.673782,230.327759,51.023605,218.107910,86.673782,218.107910" rect="50.641724,217.692154,129.354446,231.827560" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
